//! Shared plan-first contracts for normal delegation and Fusion lanes.

pub const IMPLEMENTATION_HANDOFF: &str = "Before spawning or reviving an implementation worker, the main agent must write an implementation-ready plan based on inspected code. A milestone list is not an implementation plan. Include the goal and non-goals, settled design and interfaces, owned files and existing helpers, ordered implementation steps, dependencies, regression cases, exact focused verification commands with expected outcomes, and a stopping/reporting condition. Mark unverified assumptions explicitly; resolve consequential unknowns before assigning edits. Put the relevant task plan in the subagent task/instructions (or a verified accessible plan file plus a self-contained task brief); context_refs are supporting evidence, not a substitute for the plan. Share a concise plan summary with the user and maintain milestones separately. Read-only research may be delegated before the design is settled with explicit questions and a no-edits boundary; tiny direct changes do not need a formal plan. On follow-ups, send changed decisions and scope, not the entire plan again.";

pub const WORKER_CONTRACT: &str = "Implementation worker contract: read the assigned task plan before editing. If the brief lacks the design, owned scope, acceptance criteria, or verification needed to implement safely, report NEEDS_CONTEXT with the specific gap; do not invent consequential decisions or broaden the task. Read-only research needs questions and scope, not an implementation plan. Follow the ordered steps, add a regression test for changed behavior when feasible, verify it fails for the intended reason before the fix, then run focused checks after the fix. Do not spawn implementers or reviewers; the parent owns delegation and final acceptance. Self-review the diff against the plan. Report DONE, DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, NEEDS_CONTEXT, or BLOCKED, with changed files, commands and observed results, checks not run, deviations, and reusable runtime state. A tool failure or unverified claim is not completion.";
